WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.000
-I'm Steve Higgins, and we're
about to play "Pup Quiz."

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.167
-Oh, yeah!

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:11.267
♪♪

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:15.000
-Playing tonight, we have
the host of "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.367
Mr. Jimmy Fallon!

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.968
And from "The Big Bang Theory,"

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.300
the lovely Kaley Cuoco-Sweeting!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.334
And this is the first puppy
up for grabs...

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.934
Mr. Gary Frick Jr.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:34.133
-Aww.
-Here's how the game works.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.033
I'll be asking both of you
animal trivia questions.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.767
If you answer correctly, you win
a golden retriever puppy.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.601
If you answer incorrectly,
your opponent gets the puppy.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.033
-Oh, my God.
I can't take it.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.968
-The most puppies at the end
of the game...

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.634
-That's the cutest dog.
-...wins.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.334
-Oh, my God.
-Aw.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.367
Oh, my doggy. Aw.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.067
-Kaley, you're our guest,

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.701
so you'll answer
the first question

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:04.868
and see if you win or lose
Gary Frick Jr.

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.567
"Please don't lose me."

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:12.033
Kaley, what breed of dog
is Scooby-Doo?

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.667
A, German shepherd,

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.701
B, a bloodhound,

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.200
or, C, Great Dane?

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:20.767
-Great Dane.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.501
-Great Dane, that is correct!

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:28.300
-Ah!
-You win Gary Frick Jr.!

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.901
-Oh, good dog?
-The score is 1-0.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.634
Alright, the next question
for you, Jimmy.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.067
Which of these birds...

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.100
-Ooh, I'm great with birds.
-You are?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.934
So you've given
many people the bird?

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.868
-You got a Scooby-Doo question.
Yeah. Here we go.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.667
What bird is what?
-Yeah, hello.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:45.000
Which bird is native
to New Zealand?

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.267
A, the whooping crane.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:50.234
B, the rough-faced shag.
-Uh-huh?

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:54.834
-Or, C, the brown trembler.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:58.067
Boy, take a selfie, right,
with that one.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:00.934
-You will never get this.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.767
-I'm gonna say
the New Zealand --

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.601
It's a trick question here.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:09.067
I think it's gonna be
the brown trembler.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.234
-The brown trembler.
That is wrong!

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.834
[ Buzzer ]
-Yes!

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.434
-It is the rough-faced shag.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.734
And Mary Kennedy goes to Kaley!

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:18.734
-Oh, my gosh.
-Oh, my --

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:24.634
-Oh!
Look at those puppies.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:25.968
-What? What?

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.501
-What?
-What'd you say?

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.000
-I said,
"Look at those puppies."

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.367
-No, Higgins.
Higgins, Higgins, Higgins.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.701
-Oh, do you hear that sound?
[ Dogs barking ]

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.434
That means it's time
for Double Puppardy...

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.267
-Did you hear that sound?

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.667
-...where the questions
are worth two puppies.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:41.901
-Did you hear that sound?

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.067
-Oh, how cute.
-Kaley!

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.367
-No, you didn't hear the sound,

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:46.701
did you, little schmoopy-poopy?

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.434
-Kaley.
-Yes?

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.634
-In 2008...
-Oh, God.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:54.467
-...what animal was knighted
by the king of Norway...

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:56.901
-If you get this -- Come on!
-...for distinguished service

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:59.767
in the Norwegian Royal Guard?

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.901
Was it A, a "si-lion"?

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.701
B...
-Oh, my God.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.000
-...a horse.
-Sea lion.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.200
-Oh, sea lion.
-Sea lion.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.400
-Oh, A, sea lion.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.834
Oh, I see.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.467
Was it a sea lion?
Got it.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.100
Thank you.
-Yeah, no problem.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.234
-B, horse, or C, penguin?

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.434
-It's just --
It's got to be a horse.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.567
-Is that your final answer?
-Yes.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.968
-Ooh, that is wrong!
It is a penguin!

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:29.367
Jimmy wins Kyle McAdams
and Lisa Armstrong!

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.501
-Hi!

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:31.934
-♪ Double puppy ♪

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.534
♪ Double puppy ♪
-Hi, guys! Yeah!

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:34.534
Hi, hi, hi.

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:36.767
-Oh, my God.
-Oh, hi, buddy.

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.400
Hi. Oh, my God.
They smell like puppies.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.868
-They do! They do! They do!
-They smell like puppies.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.400
Oh, my gosh, guys.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.868
You're so much better
than those other puppies.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.734
-Oh, my God.
-So much better.

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.868
-Alright, Jimmy,
this question is for you.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:50.968
-Oh, my God.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.267
-Which of these
recording artists

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:56.868
does not have a species
of wasp named after them?

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:58.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.934
Which of these recording artists

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.200
does not have a species
of wasp named after them?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.767
Is it A, Shakira,

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.033
B, Madonna,

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.400
or C, Lady "Guh-ga"?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.167
-I think it's "Ga-ga."

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:16.033
-Gaga? I'm sorry. C, Lady Gaga?
-Wasp.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.300
-I don't understand
the question.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.534
-Madonna could be a name
of a wasp, right?

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:20.701
-Two of these people have wasps
named after them.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:21.934
One does not.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.634
-Shakira doesn't sound
like a name of a wasp.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.601
Oh, maybe it does.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.367
-One of them
does not have a wasp.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.434
-I think Lady Gaga
would not have a wasp.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:30.834
That would not be
a name of a wasp.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.801
-Is that your final answer?
-Yes.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.801
-Well, then you're wrong!
-What?

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:38.167
-It is -- Madonna does not
have a wasp named after her.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.767
-What, does she have a bee
named after her?

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:40.968
I mean --
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.968
-Roger Blaine
and Ted Mooney, get out here!

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.634
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:46.901
-This -- I could die.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.167
I could die and just --
This is it.

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.000
This is it for me.
This is it.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.300
[ Dog barking ]

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.300
-Oh, my God.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.267
-Kaley.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:58.000
-This is for two more puppies.
-I can't talk right now.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.501
-In 1947, what type of animal

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:03.334
became the first
to be launched into space?

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:04.868
-What do you think it is,
schnoody?

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:08.334
-Was it A, a rhesus monkey?
-Schnoopy?

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:09.334
-What do you think?

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:12.434
-B, a fruit fly?

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:15.968
Or C, a golden retriever?

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.801
Launched into space, 1947?

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.467
-Do you think
it was one of you, schmoopy?

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.801
-1947.
-What do you think?

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.033
Oh, I love you, too.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:24.267
Oh, yeah.
Oh, yes.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.734
I have to answer now.
Oh, it's got to be you.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.067
Okay, it's you.
It's the golden retriever.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.067
It's got to be
a golden retriever.

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:29.968
-Is that your answer?
-Yes.

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:32.968
-You are very much wrong.
It was a fruit fly!

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.601
Jimmy, you get Fred Winston
and Michelle Anderson!

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.601
-What?
-Yeah!

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.467
-Michelle Anderson?
What a name.

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:42.501
-That's Michelle.
-Michelle Anderson.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:43.968
-Hi, Michelle Anderson.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.801
Fred Winston.
Come here, Fred. Hi.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.067
-Oh, Fred.

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.901
-Oh, my goodness.
Look at these guys.

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:50.634
Hi, guys.
-Oh, you know what?

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.868
[ Dog barking ]

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.868
That sound means it's time
for Final Puppardy.

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:58.467
-You keep hearing the sound
before the sound happens.

00:05:58.467 --> 00:05:59.934
Very interesting.

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:02.567
-I'm prescient.
I know when the sound is coming.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.934
That sound means it's time
for Final Puppardy.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:09.167
This is for all your
opponent's puppies and the game.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.501
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:13.300
-Pick up the boards and markers
next to you.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.367
-Guys, stop eating
the microphone.

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:16.734
-Here, I'll help you out.
There you go.

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.701
You'll write down the answer.
-Don't worry, you guys.

00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:20.834
-Whoever's closest...
-Sorry, dudes.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.167
-...to the correct answer
is the "Pup Quiz" champion.

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:24.801
-Don't worry.
-Here is the question.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:28.234
-Okay, got you.
-Don't worry, babies.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.400
Don't worry. You won't have to
go to Uncle Jimmy Fallon.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.968
-How old was the oldest
goldfish that ever lived?

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:38.334
You have 10 seconds
starting now.

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.834
[ Dogs barking to tune
of "Jeopardy!" theme ]

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:42.734
-How old was the oldest goldfish
that ever lived?

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:44.901
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.767
-Ow. Ow!

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:48.100
-He bit you?
-You bit me!

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.234
Oh, my God.
Am I bleeding?

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:53.234
-Did you write anything down?
-Am I bleeding?

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.434
-Boy, he gave you a hickey!

00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:57.400
-He gave me a hickey.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:58.868
-He really bit you!

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.300
-He did, huh?
-He really got you.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.501
Here, I'll take him if you want.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.133
-I see your answer, 42.
-Oh!

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.467
No, I didn't!

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:09.634
-How old is the oldest --
-Oldest goldfish ever to live?

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:11.634
Alright, Jimmy,
what did you write?

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:12.901
-20 years old.

00:07:12.901 --> 00:07:14.267
-I put 42.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.601
-Ooh, the correct answer is 43.

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:18.133
Kaley, you are the winner!

00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:20.534
[ Bell dinging ]

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.400
You win all the puppies!

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.300
-How would you get that?

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.834
-Thank you! Oh.

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:28.100
-Guys, our thanks
to Kaley Cuoco-Sweeting

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.400
and all these adorable puppies.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.701
-Ben Affleck!

00:07:30.701 --> 00:07:34.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.801
Now, all of our puppies...
[ Audience awws ]

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:39.267
tonight have dressed up
as their favorite superheroes.

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:40.567
[ Audience awws ]
-Whoo!

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:43.267
-And this is the first puppy
up for grabs.

00:07:43.267 --> 00:07:47.067
In the role of the Batman
himself, it's Gary Frick Jr.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:49.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey, buddy.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:52.601
-Here's how the game works --
I will be asking you

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.934
trivia questions
based on animal things.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:56.234
And if
you answer them correctly,

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:59.200
you win
a golden retriever puppy.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.767
[ Audience cheers ]
If --

00:08:00.767 --> 00:08:02.367
-Based on animal things?
-Yes, animal things.

00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:03.934
-Things.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:05.901
-You answer them incorrectly,
your opponent gets the puppy.

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:08.033
Now, most puppies
at the end of the game

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:10.801
is the "Pup Quiz" winner.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:11.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:11.968 --> 00:08:14.334
-Now, Ben,
since you're our guest,

00:08:14.334 --> 00:08:16.400
you are up first --
this question is for you.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.067
-Okay. All right.

00:08:18.067 --> 00:08:21.200
-In the DC comic series --
-Oh, forget it.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.234
[ Light laughter ]
-What was the name

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:26.868
of Batmine's -- Batman's canine
crime-fighting partner?

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:29.968
Was it --
A, Rex the Wonder Dog,

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:32.534
B, Ace the Bat-Hound,

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:34.634
or C, Batdog?

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:36.467
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:08:36.467 --> 00:08:39.000
I -- You know, I'm just going
to go with Batdog.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.234
-Batdog. Judges?

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:41.467
No!
-No!

00:08:41.467 --> 00:08:43.367
[ Buzzer ]
-It was Ace.

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:44.667
-Ace.
-Ace. The Wonder Hound.

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:47.467
Jimmy, you win Gary Frick Jr.
-Oh, no!

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:49.567
-[ Chuckles ]
[ Applause ]

00:08:49.567 --> 00:08:50.534
-Wow!

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.501
-He's Batman.

00:08:52.501 --> 00:08:54.734
-Aww!

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.567
-That's got to hurt.
-It stings.

00:08:56.567 --> 00:08:57.834
That was in my wheelhouse.
-That stings.

00:08:57.834 --> 00:08:59.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.300
I should have --
-How do you like them apples?

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.367
-...one of the specials now.

00:09:02.367 --> 00:09:04.200
-Jimmy,
next question is for you.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.667
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:09.434
-Which one of these birds --
Which one of these birds...

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:12.467
-What?
-...is native to the forests...

00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:13.901
-What? Are you kidding me?

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:16.033
-...of South America?
-What?

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.200
[ Laughing ] How did he --
-Is it...

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.300
-What?!
-...A...

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.934
-He got,
"What's Batman's dog called?"

00:09:19.934 --> 00:09:22.701
-...the shaft-tail finch...
-I don't know.

00:09:22.701 --> 00:09:26.834
-...B,
the white-bellied bustard,

00:09:26.834 --> 00:09:29.701
or C, the purple honeycreeper?

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:31.467
Which one?
Just take a guess.

00:09:31.467 --> 00:09:33.534
It's not this bird.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:34.767
-Which one of these birds
is native --

00:09:34.767 --> 00:09:36.267
-Jimmy, this is a bird --
it's not this bird.

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:37.901
-Yeah, I know.
I'm not looking.

00:09:37.901 --> 00:09:39.634
I'm not --
I'm not looking on purpose.

00:09:39.634 --> 00:09:41.267
[ Light laughter ]
All right. Yeah, thank you.

